{
  "esm": "2.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "table_interp",
    "description": "Linear and bilinear interpolation into a table that is NOT a literal constant -- a column profile, a coupled wind field, any shaped parameter or observed -- with the semantics of the standard-library templates `linear` and `bilinear` of esm:std/interp.esm, for the cases those single-lookup templates do not cover. FOR A SINGLE LOOKUP USE esm:std/interp.esm: its `linear(table, axis, x, n)` and `bilinear(table, axis_x, axis_y, x, y, nx, ny)` are pure AST (faq counts and the index op) and already take run-time tables and axes; this library does not repeat them. WHAT THIS LIBRARY ADDS. (a) A SHARED BRACKET: a template is pure substitution, so std `linear` recomputes the bracket sum at every place the index is used, for every table. When several tables share an axis and query point (u, v and theta on one set of base heights), compute the bracket ONCE as an observed with bracket_index and hand it to interp_linear_bracketed / interp_bilinear_bracketed, which only gather and blend; the Rust interpreter re-evaluates every substituted copy cell by cell, so sharing the bracket saves that work for every table after the first. (b) A PER-ROW AXIS: bracket_index_in_row, bracket_weight_in_row and interp_linear_bracketed_in_row look up row `row` of a two-dimensional axis[row, k] and table[row, k] -- an axis that differs from cell to cell, such as a sectional size distribution's per-cell section volumes, which a binding cannot slice into std `linear`'s one-dimensional axis. THE ALGORITHM is std's, step for step. (1) The bracket: the lower bracketing index is the number of axis levels at or below the query point, a sum of indicators over the axis -- for a strictly increasing axis that count IS the largest index k with axis[k] <= x -- held to [1, n-1] so the gather is always in range (outside that range the result comes from the clamp, and the held index only keeps the unused blend finite). (2) The gather of the two bracketing table and axis entries. (3) One linear blend in the order std pins: w = (x - axis[i]) / (axis[i+1] - axis[i]), then table[i] + w (table[i+1] - table[i]). Clamping matches std, including its difference between the forms: the 1-D forms return the END TABLE VALUE when x <= axis[1] or x >= axis[n], while the 2-D form clamps the QUERY COORDINATE to the axis range and then blends (at the top edge that is i = n-1 with w = 1). A NaN query falls through every comparison, counts zero levels, takes i = 1 and propagates NaN through w. Verified bit-identical to std `linear` and `bilinear` (tolerance abs 0, rel 0) by lib/tests/table_interp_checks.esm at 10 query points covering both clamps on each axis, both axis ends, knots and interior points, with the tables and axes supplied as shaped parameters and as observeds computed from parameters. The index symbol of the bracket sum is named `k_bracket` so it cannot capture an index symbol of the expression a caller binds as the query point.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "interpolation",
      "expression-templates"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "EarthSciAST standard library esm:std/interp.esm (docs/static/lib/interp.esm): the `linear` and `bilinear` templates whose bracket, clamp and pinned evaluation order these templates reproduce."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "bracket_index": {
      "params": [
        "axis",
        "x",
        "n"
      ],
      "description": "Lower bracketing index of x on the strictly increasing axis (n entries): the number of axis levels at or below x, held to [1, n-1]. Clamping x to the axis range first does not change it, so the same index serves interp_linear_bracketed and interp_bilinear_bracketed. Compute it once per query point as an observed when several tables share an axis and query (u, v and theta on one set of base heights), and hand it to the bracketed forms.",
      "body": {
        "op": "min",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "max",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "faq",
                "output_idx": [],
                "reduce": "+",
                "args": [
                  "axis"
                ],
                "ranges": {
                  "k_bracket": [
                    1,
                    "n"
                  ]
                },
                "expr": {
                  "op": "ifelse",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "<=",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "index",
                          "args": [
                            "axis",
                            "k_bracket"
                          ]
                        },
                        "x"
                      ]
                    },
                    1,
                    0
                  ]
                }
              },
              1
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
              "n",
              1
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "bracket_index_in_row": {
      "params": [
        "axis",
        "row",
        "x",
        "n"
      ],
      "description": "bracket_index on row `row` of a two-dimensional axis table axis[row, k] (n entries per row): the number of entries of that row at or below x, held to [1, n-1]. For an axis that differs from cell to cell -- a sectional size distribution's per-cell section volumes -- where bracket_index's one-dimensional axis cannot be sliced out by a binding. Finish the lookup with bracket_weight_in_row or interp_linear_bracketed_in_row.",
      "body": {
        "op": "min",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "max",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "faq",
                "output_idx": [],
                "reduce": "+",
                "args": [
                  "axis"
                ],
                "ranges": {
                  "k_bracket": [
                    1,
                    "n"
                  ]
                },
                "expr": {
                  "op": "ifelse",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "<=",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "index",
                          "args": [
                            "axis",
                            "row",
                            "k_bracket"
                          ]
                        },
                        "x"
                      ]
                    },
                    1,
                    0
                  ]
                }
              },
              1
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
              "n",
              1
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "bracket_weight": {
      "params": [
        "axis",
        "x",
        "i_lo"
      ],
      "description": "Fractional position of x between axis[i_lo] and axis[i_lo+1]: (x - axis[i_lo]) / (axis[i_lo+1] - axis[i_lo]).",
      "body": {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
              "x",
              {
                "op": "index",
                "args": [
                  "axis",
                  "i_lo"
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "index",
                "args": [
                  "axis",
                  {
                    "op": "+",
                    "args": [
                      "i_lo",
                      1
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "index",
                "args": [
                  "axis",
                  "i_lo"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "bracket_weight_in_row": {
      "params": [
        "axis",
        "row",
        "x",
        "i_lo"
      ],
      "description": "bracket_weight on row `row` of a two-dimensional axis table axis[row, k]: (x - axis[row, i_lo]) / (axis[row, i_lo+1] - axis[row, i_lo]), the weight that goes with i_lo = bracket_index_in_row(axis, row, x, n).",
      "body": {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
              "x",
              {
                "op": "index",
                "args": [
                  "axis",
                  "row",
                  "i_lo"
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "index",
                "args": [
                  "axis",
                  "row",
                  {
                    "op": "+",
                    "args": [
                      "i_lo",
                      1
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "index",
                "args": [
                  "axis",
                  "row",
                  "i_lo"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "lerp": {
      "params": [
        "lo",
        "hi",
        "frac"
      ],
      "description": "Linear blend lo + frac (hi - lo), the order std linear / bilinear pin (exact at frac = 0).",
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          "lo",
          {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "frac",
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  "hi",
                  "lo"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "clamp_to_axis": {
      "params": [
        "axis",
        "x",
        "n"
      ],
      "description": "x held to the axis range [axis[1], axis[n]]: std bilinear's per-axis clamp.",
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "<=",
            "args": [
              "x",
              {
                "op": "index",
                "args": [
                  "axis",
                  1
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "index",
            "args": [
              "axis",
              1
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": ">=",
                "args": [
                  "x",
                  {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "axis",
                      "n"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "index",
                "args": [
                  "axis",
                  "n"
                ]
              },
              "x"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "interp_linear_bracketed": {
      "params": [
        "table",
        "axis",
        "x",
        "i_lo",
        "n"
      ],
      "description": "std linear(table, axis, x, n) for a run-time table and axis of n entries, given i_lo = bracket_index(axis, x, n): table[1] for x <= axis[1], table[n] for x >= axis[n], otherwise lerp(table[i_lo], table[i_lo+1], bracket_weight(axis, x, i_lo)).",
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "<=",
            "args": [
              "x",
              {
                "op": "index",
                "args": [
                  "axis",
                  1
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "index",
            "args": [
              "table",
              1
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": ">=",
                "args": [
                  "x",
                  {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "axis",
                      "n"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "index",
                "args": [
                  "table",
                  "n"
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "apply_expression_template",
                "args": [],
                "name": "lerp",
                "bindings": {
                  "lo": {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "table",
                      "i_lo"
                    ]
                  },
                  "hi": {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "table",
                      {
                        "op": "+",
                        "args": [
                          "i_lo",
                          1
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "frac": {
                    "op": "apply_expression_template",
                    "args": [],
                    "name": "bracket_weight",
                    "bindings": {
                      "axis": "axis",
                      "x": "x",
                      "i_lo": "i_lo"
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "interp_linear_bracketed_in_row": {
      "params": [
        "table",
        "axis",
        "row",
        "x",
        "i_lo",
        "n"
      ],
      "description": "std linear(table[row, :], axis[row, :], x, n) for run-time two-dimensional tables table[row, k] and axis[row, k] (n entries per row), given i_lo = bracket_index_in_row(axis, row, x, n): table[row, 1] for x <= axis[row, 1], table[row, n] for x >= axis[row, n], otherwise lerp(table[row, i_lo], table[row, i_lo+1], bracket_weight_in_row(axis, row, x, i_lo)). The per-row counterpart of interp_linear_bracketed, with the same end-value clamp.",
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "<=",
            "args": [
              "x",
              {
                "op": "index",
                "args": [
                  "axis",
                  "row",
                  1
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "index",
            "args": [
              "table",
              "row",
              1
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": ">=",
                "args": [
                  "x",
                  {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "axis",
                      "row",
                      "n"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "index",
                "args": [
                  "table",
                  "row",
                  "n"
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "apply_expression_template",
                "args": [],
                "name": "lerp",
                "bindings": {
                  "lo": {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "table",
                      "row",
                      "i_lo"
                    ]
                  },
                  "hi": {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "table",
                      "row",
                      {
                        "op": "+",
                        "args": [
                          "i_lo",
                          1
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "frac": {
                    "op": "apply_expression_template",
                    "args": [],
                    "name": "bracket_weight_in_row",
                    "bindings": {
                      "axis": "axis",
                      "row": "row",
                      "x": "x",
                      "i_lo": "i_lo"
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "interp_bilinear_bracketed": {
      "params": [
        "table",
        "axis_x",
        "axis_y",
        "x",
        "y",
        "i_lo",
        "j_lo",
        "nx",
        "ny"
      ],
      "description": "std bilinear(table, axis_x, axis_y, x, y, nx, ny) for a run-time table[i, j] at (axis_x[i], axis_y[j]) with nx x ny entries, given i_lo = bracket_index(axis_x, x, nx) and j_lo = bracket_index(axis_y, y, ny): clamp each query coordinate to its axis, take its weight in the bracketing cell, and blend along x at rows j_lo and j_lo+1, then along y.",
      "body": {
        "op": "apply_expression_template",
        "args": [],
        "name": "bilinear_at_bracket",
        "bindings": {
          "table": "table",
          "i_lo": "i_lo",
          "j_lo": "j_lo",
          "wx": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "bracket_weight",
            "bindings": {
              "axis": "axis_x",
              "x": {
                "op": "apply_expression_template",
                "args": [],
                "name": "clamp_to_axis",
                "bindings": {
                  "axis": "axis_x",
                  "x": "x",
                  "n": "nx"
                }
              },
              "i_lo": "i_lo"
            }
          },
          "wy": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "bracket_weight",
            "bindings": {
              "axis": "axis_y",
              "x": {
                "op": "apply_expression_template",
                "args": [],
                "name": "clamp_to_axis",
                "bindings": {
                  "axis": "axis_y",
                  "x": "y",
                  "n": "ny"
                }
              },
              "i_lo": "j_lo"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "bilinear_at_bracket": {
      "params": [
        "table",
        "i_lo",
        "j_lo",
        "wx",
        "wy"
      ],
      "description": "The bilinear blend in the cell [i_lo, i_lo+1] x [j_lo, j_lo+1] with weights wx, wy, in std bilinear's pinned order: row_j = lerp(table[i_lo, j_lo], table[i_lo+1, j_lo], wx), row_jp1 = lerp(table[i_lo, j_lo+1], table[i_lo+1, j_lo+1], wx), result = lerp(row_j, row_jp1, wy).",
      "body": {
        "op": "apply_expression_template",
        "args": [],
        "name": "lerp",
        "bindings": {
          "lo": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "lerp",
            "bindings": {
              "lo": {
                "op": "index",
                "args": [
                  "table",
                  "i_lo",
                  "j_lo"
                ]
              },
              "hi": {
                "op": "index",
                "args": [
                  "table",
                  {
                    "op": "+",
                    "args": [
                      "i_lo",
                      1
                    ]
                  },
                  "j_lo"
                ]
              },
              "frac": "wx"
            }
          },
          "hi": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "lerp",
            "bindings": {
              "lo": {
                "op": "index",
                "args": [
                  "table",
                  "i_lo",
                  {
                    "op": "+",
                    "args": [
                      "j_lo",
                      1
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              "hi": {
                "op": "index",
                "args": [
                  "table",
                  {
                    "op": "+",
                    "args": [
                      "i_lo",
                      1
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "+",
                    "args": [
                      "j_lo",
                      1
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              "frac": "wx"
            }
          },
          "frac": "wy"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
